    <string name="home_plug_help">Plug a supported spectrometer into the phone\'s USB-C port with a data-capable OTG cable (micro-USB units need a micro-USB to USB-C OTG cable), or turn on the simulator in Setup.</string>
    <string name="home_btn_retry">Retry connection</string>
    <string name="home_about">PocketSpectro turns an Android phone into a portable console for Ocean Optics USB spectrometers, connected directly to the phone\'s USB-C port. It controls the spectrometer, shows live spectra in counts, absorbance or transmittance/reflectance with dark, reference, averaging, smoothing and nonlinearity correction, and logs GPS-tagged spectra for later analysis. With a near-infrared spectrometer that covers 766–770 nm, a fire-detection mode watches for the potassium emission doublet that burning vegetation produces, with an audible alarm and a map of detections, for hand-held or vehicle-based surveys.</string>
    <string name="home_developer">Developer</string>
    <string name="home_rfsat">RFSAT Limited is a non-profit research and development SME based in Dublin, Ireland, with a research office in Athens, Greece. It carries out applied research and technology development under national and EU funding programmes, including Horizon Europe, spanning digital signal processing, micro-embedded sensing, autonomous systems, GNSS positioning, and environmental and e-Health monitoring.</string>
